Data Type [Variable]
Select the data type of the Variable you are creating from the drop-down list.
Remarks
You can use any of the supported Data Types.
• For a Variable of data type object, you have to type the path to and the name of the object into the text
box Value. The starting point of the relative path is the Frame into which the Variable is inserted. Or you
can click 
  and select the object in the dialog Select Object.
Instead of typing in the path of the object or of selecting the object, you can now also drag the object
onto the Variable and drop it there. Plant Simulation then inserts a reference to the object.
• To use the data type time with a random number distribution, select the data type randtime, and type
in the parameters of the distribution function, as the data type Time only accepts constant values.
Data Type [Variable]
11-3766 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Then initialize the randtime value before accessing it, for example with the method rollDice which
determines the next random number that the Variable uses.
Note
For the list data types (table, list, stack, queue) you can use the method unshare.
• For the Data Type [user-defined attribute] > real, length, weight, time, speed, and acceleration you
can type in the number of Decimal Places and Integer Places.
