Assigning a Value to a Variable
When assigning a new value to the Variable, this value has to be compatible with the active data type of
the Variable.
Remarks
A value is compatible if Plant Simulation can automatically transform it into a correct value for the task.
A change of value may occur because:
• Plant Simulation cannot display digits after the decimal point and cuts them off. It transforms, for
example, the real value 3.9 into the integer value 3.
• Loss of significance occurs for great value differences. Floating point operations only save a certain
number of digits and the magnitude of a number (mantissa and exponent). Plant Simulation deletes
additional digits created during a calculation and the number does not return the expected value. This
kind of error cannot be avoided and only occurs if the difference in size is at least 107.
If you assign a Variable to a Method, keep in mind that Plant Simulation calls and executes this Method
if you only type in the name of a Method. This way the Method is returned, instead of the reference you
would like to receive. Use the reference operator & to get the required reference to a Variable of data type
object.
Syntax
Path := any
Example
Variable := Value
Variable := &MyMethod
Assigning a Value to a Variable
Plant Simulation Help 11-3791
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Calling the Contents of a Variable
If the contents of the Variable references another Variable of data type object, access the contents of that
variable by typing the name of this Variable in parenthesis.
If the contents of the Variable references a Method, typing this Method in parentheses calls the Method
itself.
Syntax
(Path)
Example
value := (Variable) + 1   // accesses the variable 
(control_gate)            // calls the method
(method)(3.4,"drill")     // calls the method with parameters
Calling the Contents of a Variable
11-3792 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Reading the Contents of a Variable
To access the contents of the Variable designated by <Path>, use its name.
Syntax
<Path>
Example
MyTable[1,1] := MyVariable
Methods of the Variable
_Methods of the Variable
The object Variable provides:
• The methods listed in the table of contents to the left.
Note
You can only access the methods of the object Variable, which refer to the object itself, via the
reference operator &. Without the operator the method will be applied to the contents of the
Variable.
Example
.MyPlant.&MyVariable.openDialog
Also compare:
